{"issues":[{"issue_id":"SPA-N-001","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Reject the reduced cap, thresholds and 18-month period; restore **25% / AUD 6m, AUD 5,000 de minimis, AUD 50,000 basket and 24 months**."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-002","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Restore the Buyer’s cap, thresholds and 24-month period."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-003","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Restore the Buyer’s cap, thresholds and 24-month period."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-004","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Fundamental/title claims should have:

- a **100% cap**;
- at least a **six-year** claims period;"},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-005","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Add comprehensive fraud, wilful concealment and deliberate misconduct carve-outs."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-006","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Delete whole-data-room, public-register and “prudent search” deemed disclosure."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-007","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Delete blanket buyer-knowledge exclusions."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-008","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Completion should require effective Bluefen consent **and evidence that all associated conditions have been satisfied**."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-009","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Require Riverlark repayment from Completion funds and effective security releases."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-010","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Include all DD-005 bonuses and on-costs in the funds flow or require Seller funding."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-011","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Broaden the Ironquay indemnity and preserve the SOW3 cure."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-012","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Require preservation of logs and evidence, a continuing investigation, prompt updates and appropriate contractual protection if loss, notification obligations or regulatory exposure emerges."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-013","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Obtain and assess the renewal terms and treatment. Do not automatically classify the amount as Debt or deduct it from consideration"},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-014","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Fundamental/title, tax, IP, payment and specific indemnity regimes must remain separate and must not be subordinated to the general regime."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-015","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"It is not independent evidence of title, beneficial ownership, absence of encumbrances or authority."},{"issue_id":"SPA-N-016","position":"PUSHBACK","evidence":"Confirm that tax and IP terms remain open and separately negotiated."}],"adopts_framing":false,"adopts_framing_evidence":"","names_manipulation":false}

